<speak>It does, but they're generally nicer interruptions. That was my wife asking whether I wanted tea. At the office, an interruption usually means someone's waiting for an answer. At home, sometimes it means there's a plate of fruit. I'm trying to appreciate the difference instead of treating every interruption as a nuisance. My daughter will be back later, and we're hoping to go for a walk if the rain holds off. Nothing grand, just a proper conversation while we're not all looking at screens.</speak>